WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.676 --> 00:00:02.782
- [MyneAndYours Artist] I don't
think it matters who I am.

00:00:02.782 --> 00:00:05.093
What really matters is the story.

00:00:05.093 --> 00:00:07.223
I try to remove myself from the equation

00:00:07.223 --> 00:00:10.329
by going under the name Myneandyours.

00:00:10.329 --> 00:00:12.984
It's me being inspired by our experiences.

00:00:12.984 --> 00:00:16.020
So, in a way I'm taking
what I feel is mine

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.770
and then I'm giving back
so it becomes yours.

00:00:21.401 --> 00:00:24.901
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:35.296 --> 00:00:38.296
(upbeat funk music)

00:00:41.118 --> 00:00:43.006
So, I've been here four years now.

00:00:43.006 --> 00:00:46.488
I grew up in London and
after 28 years in London,

00:00:46.488 --> 00:00:48.648
I felt that I needed a change.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.879
What I wanted to do was to be involved

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:52.632
in the creation of a culture,

00:00:52.632 --> 00:00:55.051
rather than just, you know, become a part of it.

00:00:55.051 --> 00:00:58.285
And I felt like Dubai is the
place that I could do that.

00:00:58.285 --> 00:01:01.604
I have Arab roots so it
was a place that I could,

00:01:01.604 --> 00:01:05.018
kind of, integrate
with, not feel too lost,

00:01:05.018 --> 00:01:09.185
but feel that I could contribute
to something interesting.

00:01:13.507 --> 00:01:15.517
When I started, I wanted an identity.

00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:17.898
I wanted a way for people
to recognize the work.

00:01:17.898 --> 00:01:20.796
What's funny about the cloud
is, it wasn't a choice.

00:01:20.796 --> 00:01:22.865
It was very much a doodle and,

00:01:22.865 --> 00:01:25.283
before I knew it, people
were connecting with it.

00:01:25.283 --> 00:01:26.838
And that's when I started to analyze

00:01:26.838 --> 00:01:29.010
the entire idea of a symbol,

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:33.177
and how you can use a
symbol to make people think.

00:01:34.846 --> 00:01:36.856
Dubai Design Ditrict, they asked me

00:01:36.856 --> 00:01:38.255
to create something crazy.

00:01:38.255 --> 00:01:40.506
And it was a perfect opportunity.

00:01:40.506 --> 00:01:43.364
I wanted to create an
immersive environment.

00:01:43.364 --> 00:01:45.135
What was great about painting the carpark

00:01:45.135 --> 00:01:48.109
was that it's in such an unlikely place.

00:01:48.109 --> 00:01:50.467
You would never expect it to be there.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.660
I love anything to do with
the universe and space.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.158
I'm always lost in this wonder

00:01:54.158 --> 00:01:58.003
of our position in the
universe and who we are.

00:01:58.003 --> 00:02:00.465
When I first proposed the idea to them,

00:02:00.465 --> 00:02:03.365
it seemed like it was easily possible.

00:02:03.365 --> 00:02:04.910
But, very quickly into the project,

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.700
we started to realize how
much trouble it actually was.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.722
And painting a ceiling just
became more and more painful

00:02:11.722 --> 00:02:14.519
the further that we went along.

00:02:14.519 --> 00:02:18.371
The project was 32 nights, 50,000 stars,

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:22.204
560 clouds, 500 stencils,
and one trip to A&amp;E.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:29.134
Once you just go a tiny
bit beneath the surface

00:02:29.134 --> 00:02:31.760
of what Dubai is, you
find out that there is

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.529
this huge creative community here,

00:02:34.529 --> 00:02:37.109
and a great group of like-minded people

00:02:37.109 --> 00:02:39.066
doing amazing things.

00:02:39.066 --> 00:02:40.149
I guess before I came here,

00:02:40.149 --> 00:02:43.232
I had no idea that that even existed.

